 "notes": [
  "Three trunk systems: West (to Clarkson WWTP), East (to G.E. Booth WWTP) and McVean (Brampton/Caledon, flows to the East system). Vol 4, s.3.1.2.",
  "Plant forecasts in Tables 8-9 assume each plant treats only its natural catchment, with no east-to-west transfer.",
  "The East-to-West Diversion trunk (WW-T-130, 2400 mm on Derry Road from Spring Creek to Highway 401 and Creditview Road) moves flow from the G.E. Booth catchment to Clarkson.",
  "G.E. Booth is rated 518 ML/d, but the capacity restoration project (WW-TR-182) recovers 40 ML/d to get back to 518, so effective capacity in 2020 was about 478 ML/d.",
  "Sewage pumping stations (Vol 4, Table 6) are already in data/peel-reports.json masterPlan.sps."
 ],
